msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:149
msgid "DNS Prefetch Domains"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:150
msgid "DNS prefetch performs only a DNS lookup of the domain name; ports do not affect the hint. Enter one HTTPS domain per line without file paths, query parameters, fragments, or credentials. Invalid lines are removed on save; an all-invalid list is cleared. Domain checks do not verify DNS destinations."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: Maximum bytes per domain list, 2: Maximum nonblank lines, 3: Maximum bytes per nonblank line.
#: includes/admin.php:164
#, php-format
msgid "Limits: %1$d bytes per list, %2$d nonblank lines, and %3$d bytes per nonblank line. Duplicate and invalid lines count toward the limit. Oversize submissions keep your previous list."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:222
msgid "Stops WordPress from adding its emoji detection script and emoji styles to every page, the admin area, and embedded posts, and from replacing emoji in feeds and emails with images from WordPress.org."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:223
msgid "Emoji still appear, drawn by the visitor's own device, which every current browser and operating system supports. On very old systems without emoji fonts, some emoji may show as empty boxes. Emoji in feeds and emails stay as characters instead of images."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:224
msgid "Removes a small inline script and its styles from every page, and the check that script runs in the browser: a small gain for visitors. No change on the server."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:227
msgid "Stops loading jQuery Migrate on the front end when a theme or plugin loads jQuery. jQuery Migrate restores functions that newer jQuery versions removed. The admin area is not changed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:228
msgid "Front-end code written for old jQuery versions can stop working, which shows as broken sliders, menus, or forms and as errors in the browser console. Check the interactive parts of the site after turning this on. Pages that do not load jQuery are not affected."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:229
msgid "One script file fewer to download and run on every page that loads jQuery: a small gain for visitors. No change on the server."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:232
msgid "Removes the small classic-theme stylesheet that WordPress adds on the front end for themes without a theme.json file. It gives the Button and File blocks their default look. Block themes never load it, so on them this setting changes nothing. The editor is not changed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:233
msgid "Buttons and File blocks in your content may lose their default spacing and colors if the theme does not style them itself. A stylesheet that another plugin loads on top of this one will not load either."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:234
msgid "Removes a few lines of CSS, usually printed inline in the page head, on classic themes: a very small gain for visitors. No change on the server."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:237
msgid "Limits the Heartbeat, a script that keeps a page in touch with the server through regular background requests. On the front end it stops the script from loading; WordPress loads it there only when a theme or plugin asks for it. On admin screens it sends a request every 120 seconds instead of every 60. The post editor, the site editor, and the Customizer keep the usual timing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:238
msgid "Front-end features that rely on the Heartbeat, such as live chat, live notifications, or front-end editing in some plugins, stop updating, and their scripts may not load. In the admin area, dashboard widgets that refresh through the Heartbeat update half as often, and the notice that your login has expired can appear up to two minutes later. Post locking and autosave in the editors are not changed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:239
msgid "Each Heartbeat request loads WordPress in full on the server and is never served from a page cache. Halving them on admin screens, and removing them from the front end, saves server work, which adds up when several people keep the admin area open. Visitors see no difference in page speed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:242
msgid "Stops the block editor from loading patterns from the WordPress.org Pattern Directory: the general and featured patterns, and the directory patterns a theme asks for. Patterns that come with your theme, your plugins, or WordPress itself, and the patterns you create, stay available."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:243
msgid "The pattern inserter shows far fewer ready-made patterns, because most of the patterns it offers come from the directory. Patterns already used in your content are not changed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:244
msgid "Saves the requests the server makes to WordPress.org when the editor loads patterns, and the stored copies of their results, which are refreshed about every hour. The editor's pattern list can open faster. No change on the front end."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:247
msgid "Removes the generator tag that names your WordPress version from the page head and from your RSS, Atom, and other feeds. Version numbers on script and stylesheet addresses, and export files, are left as they are."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:248
msgid "Hides the version from casual inspection and from scanners that read the tag. It is not real protection, because the version can be worked out in other ways; keeping WordPress up to date matters far more. Nothing on the site looks different."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:249
msgid "Removes one line from each page and feed. No measurable speed change."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:252
msgid "Removes the Really Simple Discovery (RSD) link from the page head. Old desktop blogging programs used it to find the site's XML-RPC address."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:253
msgid "A blogging program that relies on this link may need the XML-RPC address entered by hand. XML-RPC itself keeps working; only the link is removed. Most sites notice no difference."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:254
msgid "Removes one line from each page. No measurable speed change."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:257
msgid "Removes the shortlink, the short ?p=123 address of a post, from the page head and from the Link header that WordPress sends with each page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:258
msgid "Shortlinks still work when someone uses them; they are only no longer advertised. A tool that reads the shortlink from the page uses the full address instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:259
#: includes/admin.php:269
msgid "Removes one line from each page and one response header. No measurable speed change."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:262
msgid "Stops WordPress from printing a small inline style for the classic Recent Comments widget. WordPress prints it only on classic themes that support widgets."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:263
msgid "The widget's links may look slightly different if your theme relied on that style. Block themes and the Latest Comments block are not affected."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:264
msgid "Removes a few bytes of CSS from pages that show the widget. No measurable speed change."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:267
msgid "Removes the link to the site's REST API address from the page head and from the Link header that WordPress sends with each page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:268
msgid "The REST API keeps working: the block editor, mobile apps, and plugins that use it are not affected. Only the advertised address is removed, which a few tools and services use to find the API on their own."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:272
msgid "Removes the oEmbed discovery links from the page head of posts and pages. Other sites read them to show one of your posts as an embedded card when someone pastes its link."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:273
msgid "A link to one of your posts pasted into another WordPress site, or into some apps and services, shows as a plain link instead of a card. Embedding videos, posts, and other content from other sites in your own posts keeps working."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:274
msgid "Removes two lines from each post and page. No measurable speed change."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:277
msgid "Removes the links to the site's RSS feeds, for posts, comments, and categories, tags, or authors, from the page head."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:278
msgid "The feeds keep working at their usual addresses, but browsers and feed readers can no longer find them from a page, so someone who subscribes by entering the site's address may need the feed's address instead. Leave this off if people follow the site in a feed reader."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:279
msgid "Removes a few lines from each page. No measurable speed change."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:282
msgid "Tells WordPress that AI features are not supported on this site. WordPress then does not register its built-in AI provider connectors, and refuses AI provider connectors from plugins."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:283
msgid "AI features that rely on WordPress's AI support are unavailable, including those in plugins that check for it. Connectors that are not AI providers, such as Akismet, are not affected. Setting the WP_AI_SUPPORT constant to false in wp-config.php has the same effect."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:284
msgid "No measurable speed change. WordPress only skips registering its AI provider connectors on each request."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:287
msgid "Turns off Jetpack's promotional notices, its Just-in-Time upgrade messages, and its Blaze prompts to advertise your posts. It does nothing unless Jetpack is installed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:288
msgid "Jetpack keeps working; you no longer see its upgrade and advertising prompts in the admin area. Visitors see no difference."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:289
msgid "Jetpack skips loading and showing these messages, which saves a little work and some requests in the admin area. No change on the front end."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:292
msgid "Turns off publishing by email: the mail server settings disappear from Settings > Writing and can no longer be saved, and the wp-mail.php address that collects the mail refuses requests."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:293
msgid "Nobody can publish posts by sending email to the configured mailbox. Existing posts are not affected. Leave this off if you post by email."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:294
msgid "No speed change. It closes a rarely used way into the site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:297
msgid "Adds a preconnect hint to the page head for each domain in the Preconnect Domains list, so the browser opens a connection to those servers before it needs them. Front-end pages only; the admin area and the login page are skipped."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:298
msgid "Files from those domains, such as web fonts, can start downloading sooner. A listed domain that the page does not use wastes a connection."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:299
msgid "Can save one or more network round trips the first time each listed domain is used, which helps most on slow or distant connections. Each hint costs the browser a connection, so list only the few domains that serve files a page needs early. No measurable cost on the server."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:302
msgid "The domains that get a preconnect hint while Enable Preconnect is on."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:303
msgid "Only the domains entered here get hints. The suggestions below are examples and are never added on their own."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:304
msgid "Two or three domains are usually enough. More hints compete for the browser's connections and can slow down the files that matter most."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:307
msgid "Adds a DNS prefetch hint to the page head for each domain in the DNS Prefetch Domains list, so the browser looks up those domain names before it needs them. Front-end pages only; the admin area and the login page are skipped."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:308
msgid "Requests to those domains start slightly sooner. Unlike preconnect, no connection is opened, so it suits domains that are used later or only on some pages."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:309
msgid "Saves the name lookup, often a few tens of milliseconds, the first time each listed domain is used. It costs the browser very little, even for a domain that ends up unused. No measurable cost on the server."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:312
msgid "The domains that get a DNS prefetch hint while Enable DNS Prefetch is on."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:313
msgid "Only the domains entered here get hints. The suggestion below is an example and is never added on its own."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:314
msgid "Lookups are cheap, so a longer list does little harm, but each entry only helps if pages request files from that domain."
msgstr ""

