#: includes/autoload-page.php:466
msgid "Lists the options that WordPress loads from the database on every page, largest first, and lets you stop loading the ones you select on every page. Only the option's autoload setting changes; its value stays in the database, and WordPress still reads it when code asks for it. WordPress does not record which plugin or theme created an option, so the \"Probably from\" column is an informed guess. To firm it up, search the installed code for the names on a page, or record which options pages actually read and which code reads them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/autoload-page.php:467
msgid "Code that needs a switched-off option still gets it, so a site rarely breaks; after each change the plugin loads your home page and the dashboard, and undoes the change at once if either answers with a server error. The best candidates are large options that no recorded page reads, or that no installed plugin or theme contains: those were usually left behind by a removed plugin. A plugin can switch an option back on when it saves it, and the second list shows when that has happened. Options that WordPress and this plugin need are locked. If a site still breaks, WP-CLI can undo every change, even with all plugins skipped: see the plugin's FAQ."
msgstr ""

#: includes/autoload-page.php:468
msgid "Every page loads all of these options in one query, and with a persistent object cache, such as Redis, they are kept together in one cache entry, which a very large total can push past the cache server's size limit. A smaller total makes that load faster and lighter on memory. Each option you switch off that a page still needs costs that page one extra small query when no persistent object cache is in use. Recording adds a little work to each page while it runs, and the code search reads many files once, when you ask for it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/autoload-page.php:522
msgid "When you delete Site Optimizer, it first loads every option it switched off on every page again, with the setting each one had before. Deactivating the plugin changes nothing."
msgstr ""

